                    {
                        "recommendationid": "231616234",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197966091591",
                            "num_reviews": 77,
                            "playtime_forever": 17,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 17,
                            "last_played": 1785355446
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Got this in a Fanatical (Bundlestars) bundle years ago and finally redeemed it. The first part of the game is a slow-moving walking sim which isn't reflected in the game's tags. After the initial customary tutorial showing you WASD, jump, run prompts, you're thrown into a large alien world where you just walk. And walk. And walk. You're forced to drop down where fall damage hurts you but are not given any healing. Dying sends you back to the last checkpoint which can be a lengthy walk from where you died.\n\nIf the developers are trying to evoke a stark desolate world, they could have done so without such a needlessly drawn out opening. Whatever story they're trying to tell, that seems loosely inspired by Stanisław Lem's Solaris, is seemingly wasted because of just bad pacing. There is a difference between boring your players and creating a suspenseful sense of desolation.\n\nI want the last 15 minutes of my life back.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1785356419,
